  "problem": "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4=x \\\\ -7=3+y\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | $1$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | {{field-4}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-10$ |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $1$ | {{field-1}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-10$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n.",
  "worked_solution": "First, we organize the system so that it\u2019s in the correct order and both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+0y=4 \\\\ 0x+y=-10\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
